chuckcar wrote:
> isn't called polypile because you make *a* pile?

The more objects you have in one pile, the more likely you are to lose
objects to "shuddering vibrations" or have them meld together to form a
golem.

Many piles with few items is more conservative of your items.
Few piles with many items is more conservative of your /poly charges
(or spell points).

Usually I'll do a row of 4 piles, each of which has 2 rings, 2 potions,
2 scrolls, 2 amulets, 2 magic tools, etc.  Seems to be a reasonable
compromise, but if you have multiple /poly and are going for particular
hard-to-get items then smaller piles or even individual objects can
make sense.



